{{define "content"}}
<div class="config-sub" id="page-config-rates">
{{template "config_sub_header" $}}
<h1>Model rates</h1>
<p class="sub">
  Prices in <strong>dollars per million tokens</strong>, used by the
  <a href="{{route "spend"}}">spend report</a>. Rates are not built in: published
  prices change, deployments negotiate their own, and a stale number compiled into
  the binary would look authoritative while being wrong.
</p>
<p class="sub">
  A blank field means <em>unset</em>, which is different from zero. A run whose
  model has no rate — or whose rate does not cover a token class it used — reports
  its tokens with no dollar figure, rather than a cost of $0.00 that would read as
  free. Fill in only the classes your runs actually produce: a Grok-only setup
  never needs the cache columns.
</p>
<p class="sub">
  OpenRouter publishes a public models API with per-token list prices.
  <strong>Fill blanks from OpenRouter</strong> copies those into empty cells
  (converted to dollars per million tokens). grokwork does not route through
  OpenRouter, so this is a convenience, not a bill — and a figure you already
  typed is never overwritten. Cursor models are skipped: they are not billed at
  those list rates.
</p>
<div class="section card">
  <form method="post" action="{{route "config.rates"}}">
    {{template "csrf" $}}
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Model</th>
          <th>Input</th>
          <th>Output</th>
          <th>Cache read</th>
          <th>Cache write</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range .Config.ModelRates}}
        {{/* Every row posts all five fields, blanks included: the handler matches
             rows by position, so a sparse form would shift rates onto the wrong
             model. */}}
        <tr>
          <td>
            <input type="hidden" name="model" value="{{.Model}}">
            <span class="mono">{{.Model}}</span>
            {{if .Agent}}<span class="drill-s" style="display:block">{{.Agent}}{{if not .Curated}} · from config{{end}}</span>{{else if not .Curated}}<span class="drill-s" style="display:block">from config</span>{{end}}
          </td>
          <td><input type="text" name="input" value="{{.Input}}" placeholder="unset" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-label="{{.Model}} input rate"></td>
          <td><input type="text" name="output" value="{{.Output}}" placeholder="unset" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-label="{{.Model}} output rate"></td>
          <td><input type="text" name="cacheRead" value="{{.CacheRead}}" placeholder="unset" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-label="{{.Model}} cache read rate"></td>
          <td><input type="text" name="cacheWrite" value="{{.CacheWrite}}" placeholder="unset" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-label="{{.Model}} cache write rate"></td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.75rem 0 0">
      Cache write is billed above the input rate by most providers (1.25× on
      Anthropic), so it is a separate column rather than an assumption. Cache read
      is the cheapest class and usually the largest: every agent turn after the
      first re-reads the whole prompt prefix and is charged for it again.
    </p>
    <div class="form-actions">
      <button type="submit">Save</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <form method="post" action="{{route "config.rates.openrouter"}}" data-confirm="Fill empty rate cells from OpenRouter list prices? Existing figures are left alone. Cursor models are skipped — they are not billed at those rates." data-confirm-title="Fill from OpenRouter" data-confirm-ok="Fill blanks">
    {{template "csrf" $}}
    <div class="form-actions">
      <button type="submit" class="btn-secondary">Fill blanks from OpenRouter</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>
</div>
{{end}}
